-- title:
--   Branch-norm factorisation of the y-product at a supersingular node
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a level $N \neq 0$, a perfect field $k$ of characteristic $q$ with a ring map $red : A \to k$, modular polynomial data for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence, integrality of the two degeneracy maps $\overline\alpha,\overline\beta$ at level $(N,q)$, a place specialisation $P$ and a prolongation tuple $R$ over it. Let $K \subset \overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a number field, $w$ a place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\;k\;N$ lying in $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\;q\;N\;k$, and $c$ a system of node coordinates $x,y$ in $B := R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\,K\,w$ (the functions in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ integral for both prolongations $R_1,R_2$ and for every place over $w$, and lying in the $K$-rational subfield $\mathrm{fieldOver}\,(Nq)\,K$). Let $\mathcal O := A \cap K$ and $\varpi \in \mathcal O$ be nonzero. Assumed: $B$ is local and Noetherian with maximal ideal $(\varpi, x, y)$ (constants embedded by $\mathrm{nodeConst}$); for every $g \in B$ some $g - o$ with $o \in \mathcal O$ is a non-unit; the value-integrality law at $w$, i.e. every node integer has all its values at places over $w$ in $A$; every prime strictly below a non-maximal prime of $B$ is zero; every element of $\mathrm{fieldOver}\,(Nq)\,K$ is a ratio of elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator; $\mathcal O$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $(\varpi)$. Further, $W$ is a complete discrete valuation domain with irreducible $\pi$, $E \ge 1$, and $\iota$ is a ring isomorphism from the $\mathfrak m_B$-adic completion of $B$ onto $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,W\,(\pi^E) = W[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi^E)$ carrying $\varpi$ to $\mathrm{const}\,\pi$, $x$ to $U$ times a unit $\alpha_U$ and $y$ to $V$ times a unit $\beta_V$; $\tau$ is a ring isomorphism from the completion of $\mathcal O$ onto $W$ compatible with $\iota$ on constants and with $\tau(\varpi) = \pi$; $j$ maps the completion of $\mathcal O$ into the valuation ring of the completion of $A$'s valuation, compatibly on constants. Finally $\mathfrak q$ is a nonzero prime of $B$ containing no nonzero constant, $S$ is the finite set of places $V$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V = w$ whose evaluation kernel on $B$ is exactly $\mathfrak q$, and the cardinality of $S$ equals $\sum_Q \mathrm{finrank}_W\bigl(W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^E)\big/Q\bigr)$, the sum being over the minimal primes $Q$ of the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak q$ under $\iota$ with $\mathrm{const}\,\pi \notin Q$. The conclusion is the existence of $n_Q \in \mathbb N$ and $u_Q \in W^\times$, indexed by points of the prime spectrum of the crossing model, such that for every such minimal prime $Q$ avoiding $\mathrm{const}\,\pi$ one has $\mathrm{Norm}_{W}\bigl(\iota(y) \bmod Q\bigr) = \pi^{n_Q} u_Q$, and such that in the completion of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at the valuation of $A$ the product $\prod_{V \in S} V.\mathrm{evalAt}(y)$ equals the image under $j \circ \tau^{-1}$ of $\pi^{\sum_Q n_Q} \prod_Q u_Q$, both sum and product taken over the same set of minimal primes.
--
--   This is the value-level product formula for the node coordinate $y$ at a supersingular node of $X_0(Nq)$, rewritten so that each branch contribution appears as a norm $\pi^{n_Q}u_Q$ computed in the discrete valuation ring $W$ after passing to the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^E)$; no integrality of branch depths is assumed. It refines [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.prod_evalAt_eq_prod_norm_quotient_of_forall_iff_evalAt_eq_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.prod_evalAt_eq_prod_norm_quotient_of_forall_iff_evalAt_eq_zero) and feeds the computation of the quotients of residues $\bar y$ by powers at inertia-stable nodes.
